Package: fexwine-emu
Version: 1.0-4
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: fexwine-emu contributors <kanhuiji100@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: 3300000
Depends: bubblewrap
Recommends: fonts-wqy-microhei | fonts-noto-cjk
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/kanhuiji100/fexwine-emu
Description: FEX-Emu + Wine environment to run 32/64-bit Windows programs on aarch64
 Contains a self-contained Ubuntu 22.04 (arm64) root filesystem with FEX-Emu 2610
 and Hangover Wine 11.16 including the FEX emulation backends
 (libwow64fex.dll for 32-bit x86, libarm64ecfex.dll for 64-bit x86).
 Everything runs inside a bubblewrap user-namespace sandbox, so no root and no
 password are needed at runtime, and the host glibc/libstdc++ version does not
 matter (host glibc 2.31 is fine).
 .
 Commands: wine, winecfg, wineboot, wineserver, winetricks, regedit, notepad,
 msiexec, winedbg, wineconsole, fexshell, fex, fexbash, fexemu, fex-rootfs,
 fexwine-launcher.
 .
 Windows 32-bit and 64-bit programs are supported (PE code is emulated by FEX;
 the Wine/Unix side is native arm64). Tested on Kylin V10 aarch64 with kernels
 5.4.18 and 5.10.97.
 .
 This build bundles a WebKitGTK browser so Windows programs can open http(s)
 URLs via ShellExecute/winebrowser, and ships CJK font aliases generated from
 WenQuanYi Micro Hei (family names 微软雅黑/宋体/SimSun/Tahoma ...) so Java/Swing
 programs render Chinese correctly. Java runs with JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-Xint by
 default to avoid an upstream FEX JVM JIT crash (override if you need speed).
